e_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04163278139214901,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":57.4,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0588085734308782,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.006207508128879693,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":89.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.014199999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":9.5,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Brighthouse Financial, Inc. provides annuity and life insurance products in the United States. The company operates through Annuities, Life, and Run-off segments. The Annuities segment offers variable, fixed, index-linked, and income annuities for contract holders' needs for protected wealth accumulation on a tax-deferred basis, wealth transfer, and income security. The Life segment provides term, universal, whole, and variable life products for policyholders' needs for financial security and protected wealth transfer. The Run-off segment manages universal life with secondary guarantees, structured settlements, pension risk transfer contracts, various company-owned life insurance policies, and funding agreements. Brighthouse Financial, Inc. was founded in 1863 and is headquartered in Charlotte, North Carolina.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Eric Thomas Steigerwalt | President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $4.8M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Stock-based compensation of $30K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Brighthouse Financial, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $2.4B market cap on $6.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -7% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 6.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 3.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.2% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.0) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 22% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 70/100): structural revenue/margin decline; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Financial Services peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Compared to Estimates, Brighthouse Financial (BHF) Q3 Earnings: A Look at Key Metrics","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025155/compared-to-estimates-brighthouse-financial-bhf-q3-earnings-a-look-at-key-metrics?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm-3025155","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793925002.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Brighthouse Financial (BHF) Beats Q3 Earnings Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3025133/brighthouse-financial-bhf-beats-q3-earnings-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3025133","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793923204.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Brighthouse Financial (BHF) Projected to Announce Quarterly Earnings on Thursday","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/brighthouse-financial-bhf-projected-to-announce-quarterly-earnings-on-thursday.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793786239.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Is Brighthouse Financial (BHF) A Bargain After Its Sharp Selloff?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nasdaq-bhf/brighthouse-financial/news/is-brighthouse-financial-bhf-a-bargain-after-its-sharp-sello","date":"2026-11-04","t